{"id":"zpool-destroy.8","n":"zpool-destroy","s":"8","src":{"u":{"pkg":"zfsutils-linux","ver":"2.1.5-1ubuntu6~22.04.7","repo":"jammy-updates/main","url":"http://archive.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/pool/main/z/zfs-linux/zfsutils-linux_2.1.5-1ubuntu6~22.04.7_amd64.deb","path":"/usr/share/man/man8/zpool-destroy.8.gz","sha256":"5fbb7ea81e8cf04fef9a588e2146bfb25566ffc014aa15fc23fd4cc1a87d211d","date":"May 31, 2021","origin":"OpenZFS"}},"nopt":{"u":1},"desc":"destroy ZFS storage pool","u":[["NAME","<p><b>zpool-destroy</b> — destroy ZFS storage pool</p>"],["SYNOPSIS","<table> <tr> <td><b>zpool</b></td> <td><b>destroy</b> [<b>-f</b>] <i>pool</i></td> </tr> </table>"],["DESCRIPTION","<p>Destroys the given pool, freeing up any devices for other use. This command tries to unmount any active datasets before destroying the pool.</p> <dl><dt data-o=\"\"><b>-f</b></dt><dd>Forcefully unmount all active datasets.</dd></dl>"]]}